*.xcodeproj/
# XcodeGen writes these from the `info:` / `entitlements:` blocks of
# App/project.yml, so they are generator output like the .xcodeproj beside
# them, and they matched the generator byte for byte. (A second, `Probe`, pair
# was ignored here too until that target was deleted with the rename.)
App/Vocula/Info.plist
App/Vocula/Vocula.entitlements
.build/
.swiftpm/
DerivedData/
# `scripts/notarize.sh` writes its Release build, its own DerivedData and the
# signed zips here — inside the working tree, and it was the one build output
# with no rule. A release run left a gigabyte untracked in `git status`, where
# the next `git add -A` would have swept it into a commit.
# ANCHORED, and it has to be. Unanchored `build/` matches EVERY directory of
# that name — including `Design/build/`, whose tokens.css is TRACKED. That file
# survived only because gitignore does not apply to what is already tracked, so
# rebuilding the index in a fresh checkout dropped it silently. Measured: 265
# files staged where 266 were expected.
/build/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
.idea/

# Developer-local signing overrides (see App/Signing.xcconfig).
App/Local.xcconfig
.DS_Store

# Tooling scratch output.
.playwright-mcp/
# Personal runners at the ROOT; every script this repository ships is in
# scripts/. Anchored, or this would sweep those out of the tree too.
/*.sh

# Isolated git worktrees created for subagent-driven feature work.
.worktrees/

# Every markdown file at the ROOT is a maintainer's note until it is named here.
# Anchored, so it cannot reach the tracked .md under .github/, Localization/ and
# Packaging/. The four exceptions are what a stranger is owed: how to build it,
# what it stores, that patches are not accepted, and where to report a hole.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/PRIVACY.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/SECURITY.md
docs/

# Export/import traffic for the translation loop. NOT `Localization/` — the
# glossary lives there and is committed.
Localization/*.xcloc

# Slow-test audio fixtures. They are RENDERED, not authored: four are `say`
# output in Apple-licensed voices and pl-cue.f32 carries 565 ms of
# /System/Library/Sounds/Frog.aiff. Publishing this tree under GPL-3.0 would
# re-license Apple's assets, which is not ours to do. `Cue.swift` itself is
# clean — NSSound(named:) is a runtime lookup on the user's own Mac and
# redistributes nothing; only the baked bytes were the problem.
# `scripts/make-fixtures.sh` renders them locally, and every slow suite that
# needs one is gated on its existence, so a checkout without them SKIPS rather
# than fails.
Tests/VoculaSlowTests/Fixtures/*.f32
